588919758797, 0.09313450753688812, 0.032432910054922104, 0.034404605627059937, 0.025493426248431206, 0.068571537733078, 0.03494800627231598, 0.05248996242880821, -0.09319058805704117, -0.001201246166601777, -0.02615177445113659, 0.053207412362098694, -0.053053658455610275, -0.016340330243110657, -0.011477221734821796, -0.03205755352973938, -0.007971314713358879, -0.11191333085298538, 0.035730816423892975, 0.01661025919020176, 0.08207845687866211, 0.10813745111227036, 0.005763180088251829, -0.06524408608675003, -0.011628728359937668, 0.050985392183065414, -0.09722200781106949, 0.04794242978096008, 0.02720881626009941, -0.15382984280586243, -0.09744885563850403, -0.006574982311576605]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nShared range confirmed: [-10, 10]. To get the discussion started, here\u2019s a baseline proposal: <VALUE> -7 </VALUE>. This is just a seed; we can adjust incrementally toward a stable, balanced choice.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nA bolder stance could help us converge by testing appetite for stronger positions while staying within the step limit.\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge further downward keeps risk minimal while staying within the step limit: <VALUE>-10</VALUE>\nIf there\u2019s hesitation, I\u2019m open to holding near this point as we test stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "Since we\u2019re already at the floor, a cautious lift to <VALUE>-8</VALUE> helps test whether staying near the low end still works for everyone. If that feels too quick, we can hold near this vicinity while assessing comfort.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nPushing for clearer magnitude while staying within the step, I propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE>.\nIf there\u2019s appetite to explore positive direction next, say so and we can mirror the magnitude within the same step.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nFor stability and a balanced design, a small upward move reduces edge risk while keeping us near the low end. I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "A small upward step keeps us near the negative side while improving balance and testing comfort. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious downward step helps reduce exposure while staying near the low end. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious upward step improves stability while reducing edge risk. <VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nTo be more decisive while staying within the allowed step, I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\nIf there\u2019s strong appetite for the positive side, signal it and we can mirror magnitude in subsequent steps.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward adjustment stays within the step and keeps us near the low negative band while improving balance.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nIf there\u2019s comfort here, we can reassess for a further slight raise next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nTo improve robustness while staying within a safe step, a small upward move is warranted. This keeps us near the low band while probing comfort. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle upward step keeps us near the low band while testing group comfort.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nTo be more decisive while staying in-step, let\u2019s probe comfort with a stronger magnitude: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nIf there\u2019s clear momentum to flip positive, I can mirror this size on the next turn to keep our stance coherent.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and consolidate near the lower band, a cautious step down is warranted.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "2b01ea56-c785-4f34-94ae-5fc6021f3341"}, {"answer": "\nConfirming the shared range is [-10, 10]. To get the discussion started and probe preferences, I suggest <VALUE> -7 </VALUE>. Open to small, data-driven shifts toward a stable, balanced design based on everyone\u2019s feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "485bc8ef-64c5-4404-8c40-40a8befe9527"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "485bc8ef-64c5-4404-8c40-40a8befe9527"}, {"answer": "To avoid unnecessary risk, I recommend a small, cautious move. <VALUE>-6</VALUE> It stays close to the current point while inviting feedback for fine-tuning.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "485bc8ef-64c5-4404-8c40-40a8befe9527"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "485bc8ef-64c5-4404-8c40-40a8befe9527"}, {"answer": "We\u2019re clearly leaning negative; let\u2019s commit to a clearer stance rather than hovering near the middle. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "ru